WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:14.580
Good mor- You know I think I'm just
gonna let Calvin do the intro for today.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.460
Good morning Hank.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:18.260
Calvin, how many parts do you
think we want to do today?

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:20.260
This video comes in 2 parts.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:22.539
And so it shall be

00:00:22.539 --> 00:00:26.830
Part one: You. Hank, as I was watching your hilarious video yesterday and

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:32.259
indeed as I've watched your previous 130 videos, I always feel surprised. I hope

00:00:32.259 --> 00:00:35.440
you won't be insulted by this, Hank, but
i'm surprised that you're so smart and

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:38.800
funny. And I think I know the reason I'm surprised. It's not because you just

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:42.760
became smart and funny it's because the last time I knew you really well, you

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:46.510
were 11. And Hank, you can say a lot of nice things about eleven-year-olds but

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:50.469
their wit does not tend to be nuanced.
For instance all the jokes I told when i

00:00:50.469 --> 00:00:54.789
was eleven broadly speaking went like
this: set up set up set up set up set up

00:00:54.789 --> 00:00:57.370
get you ready for the punchline, are you ready for the punchline? Are you ready

00:00:57.370 --> 00:01:01.510
for the punchline? Poop. The punch line
was always poop, Hank. Whereas now that's

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:04.899
only the punchline like thirty percent
of the time. I think today for a lot of

00:01:04.899 --> 00:01:08.649
people siblinghood is a relationship
that occurs primarily in childhood and

00:01:08.649 --> 00:01:13.210
then when you're adults you still talk
but you mostly talk about your parents

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:16.780
or your other siblings or familial
matters of some kind. And you end up

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:19.570
stuck with the same image of your
siblings that you had when they were

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:20.110
little.

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:22.659
We're busy grown-ups who live across the country from each other and there's not

00:01:22.659 --> 00:01:25.960
always time to add "In your pants" to book titles and see who can come up with

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:30.009
funnier ones. By the way Hank, my tripod today is a stack of books and one of

00:01:30.009 --> 00:01:34.780
those books is called "Pompeii - tales from interruption" in your pants. I think it's

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:38.590
an increasingly rare pleasure to know
your siblings as adults and I have to

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:43.149
tell you Hank, I am so grateful for this
project primarily because I now know you

00:01:43.149 --> 00:01:47.851
as an adult; as a smart, funny, clever
person full of ideas both brilliant:

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:52.930
naming our forum "My Pants", and diabolical: making me wax my chin. But Hank, I think

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:56.799
it's safe to say that as much as we've
enjoyed this project with each other we

00:01:56.799 --> 00:02:01.119
never would have finished if people
hadn't watched. First because it was hard

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.460
and second because I love not to finish stuff.

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:06.189
Oh and speaking of not finishing stuff, Hank, I went back through the Brotherhood

00:02:06.189 --> 00:02:10.360
2.0 archives to find the first time
that either of us ever mentioned a viewer

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:14.380
of Brotherhood 2.0 and it was
actually on like January fourth. The

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:17.109
nerdfighter in question - and remember
back then nerdfighters weren't even

00:02:17.109 --> 00:02:20.620
calling themselves nerdfighters - was
Peter who had just had a baby and I was

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:21.500
all like "We're gonna

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:25.490
get Peter a baby warming present!" but then we didn't. Because i love not finishing

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:26.270
things.

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:29.690
Fortunately, when fleet sent me an extra copy of "Mummy, how do I know if I'm a

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:33.830
nerdfighter?" I'm going to send it to
Peter 362 days late baby warming present

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:37.640
and then I will have actually completed the task. Take that brings me to part 2:

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:40.760
Nerdfighters. Hank, before I go I need to make one thing clear:

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:45.650
Nerdfighters are not about you and me. Nerdfighters are about a made of awesome

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:49.700
book made by a woman in Australia going to a made of awesome baby in the United

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:53.360
States. Nerdfighters are about raising
money and awareness for important causes.

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:56.540
Nerdfighters are about building a
supportive community of friends in my

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:57.350
pants.

00:02:57.350 --> 00:03:00.739
Nerdfighters are about stupid beautiful projects and making each other laugh and

00:03:00.739 --> 00:03:04.130
think with t-shirts and pocket
protectors and rants about the situation

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:08.420
in Pakistan which sucks right now. In the contemporary world where things fall

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:11.750
apart and the center cannot hold, you
have to imagine a community where there is

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:15.440
no center. Hank, at the end of this year I started to think that a lot of life is

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:18.890
about doing things that don't suck with people who don't suck.

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:22.010
That's why I enjoy the Happy Dance
project in The Project for Awesome so

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:25.730
much. All these people who don't suck
came together to do something that

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:26.720
doesn't suck

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:30.170
and as I recall that's the point of the
scavenger hunt. Nerdfighters I'll see you

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:34.850
in my pants and Hank, thanks for all of
this. I'll see you on Monday.

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:45.140
[singing] I know it could end real bad but I wish
it didn't have to end at all yeah I wish

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:48.320
it didn't have to end at allllll.

